  "body": "It seems that Chromium and WebKit use the rules for parsing integers, not non-negative integers. And then it's roughly similar:\n\n- Error: do nothing.\n- Value > 1: value minus 2.\n- Else: hint for `border-bottom-width: 0`.\n\nI suspect we could align Chromium and WebKit here, but it seems less risky for Gecko to align.\n\nDemo we could convert into a test: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14610\n\ncc @mfreed7 @zcorpan \n",
